WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Let's create a blog, from scratch, and publish it to the web on Quarto Pub.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.584
So inside the RStudio IDE

00:00:08.584 --> 00:00:09.553
New project, new directory

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:13.003
New Quarto Blog

00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:15.638
And then create that new session

00:00:15.638 --> 00:00:18.300
going to let it switch over to the new environment. 

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.302
And now we're going to test building the blog. 

00:00:20.302 --> 00:00:22.698
Quarto has gone ahead and created a bunch of different files. 

00:00:22.698 --> 00:00:26.657
These create the quarto blog and all the "hello world" examples. 

00:00:26.657 --> 00:00:30.946
You can see those locally by clicking the the build tab. 

00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:32.946
Render website

00:00:32.946 --> 00:00:34.946
That will build the blog and you can see that we have a functioning blog in the preview. 

00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:36.866
Post with code (blog post example), you can see we have an about me page. 

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:41.623
we can work with this locally but we can publish this to the web 

00:00:41.623 --> 00:00:44.258
inside rstudio I can go down to the console pane

00:00:44.258 --> 00:00:47.998
 Click over to the Terminal.

00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:50.779
To the Quarto Command Line Interface (CLI)

00:00:50.779 --> 00:00:52.940
And type quarto publish

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.637
This is going to provide me with a few options. you can publish to Quarto Pub which is a free service we provide. 

00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:59.276
I'm going to do that because I already have it set up.

00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:01.276
It's going to ask which account you want to use. I'm going to do that because I already have an account. 

00:01:01.276 --> 00:01:03.276
But if you don't have an account it will ask you to sign up. 

00:01:03.276 --> 00:01:07.525
Press enter and it's going to publish that to Quarto Pub with a specific name

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:13.190
in this case test blog 2

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:14.541
I'll click enter and it's going to use all that information and put it to the web. 
while it does this it's going to build the website again, 

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:22.467
all the blog posts all put together, re-render all those different components, and then ship it out to the wild. 

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:28.727
in the span of this little speed run, we can go from no blog, to new blog, to blog on the internet, and go and look at and share it 

00:01:28.727 --> 00:01:37.573
and now we have a blog post to share and a blog we can share with the world 

00:01:37.573 --> 00:01:41.016
to learn more about using quarto, as a computational notebook, for technical and scientific communication pls check out the resources at quarto-dot-org. 

00:01:41.016 --> 00:01:49.501
THANKS! 

